        "mission_intent": "Team, I need us to build out a complete specification for our audit information protection controls aligned with NIST 800-53 Rev. 5, specifically covering the enhanced requirements around dual authorization, read-only access restrictions, and cross-platform audit storage. For dual authorization, the spec must define which audit functions require two-person approval before execution, identify the authorized individuals or roles, and establish a rotation schedule for those duties\u2014while also carving out explicit exceptions for situations requiring immediate response to protect public or environmental safety. For the read-only access enhancement, we need to define the specific subset of privileged users and roles who will be granted read-only access to audit information, with the rationale being to limit potential damage such as deletion of audit records to conceal unauthorized activity. For the cross-OS storage requirement, the spec should identify which system components running a different operating system from the audited systems will serve as the designated audit storage targets, and document how this architectural separation reduces the risk of compromise. Each control enhancement should reference its related controls\u2014particularly AC-3 for dual authorization\u2014and map to our existing SIEM infrastructure and SOC workflows. Please have the draft specification ready for review by the end of next week so we can incorporate it into our upcoming audit readiness package.",
